00:31:24,340 --> 00:31:27,760
We now return to chocolate on Modern Marvels.

370
00:31:31,100 --> 00:31:35,560
Chocolate can taste especially great when wrapped around other stuff that tastes great.

371
00:31:35,561 --> 00:31:42,240
For the everyman, perhaps a peanut butter cup.

372
00:31:42,241 --> 00:31:48,120
For the connoisseur, a fine, handmade truffle, traditionally a soft chocolate center coated

373
00:31:48,121 --> 00:31:54,640
in hard chocolate or cocoa powder.

374
00:31:54,641 --> 00:31:59,940
But the frugal aficionado can split the difference and buy truffles expertly mass produced by

375
00:31:59,941 --> 00:32:01,060
lint and sprungleaf.

376
00:32:05,560 --> 00:32:12,560
We see Lindt as a daily affordable luxury.

377
00:32:12,561 --> 00:32:19,560
We don't believe that good chocolate is only designed or made for certain consumers.

378
00:32:19,561 --> 00:32:26,560
We believe that everybody deserves to experience the ultimate chocolate experience.

379
00:32:26,561 --> 00:32:32,560
Lindt fastidiously controls the entire process in a manner worthy of the Swiss,

380
00:32:32,561 --> 00:32:35,400
the world's heaviest consumers of chocolate.

381
00:32:37,460 --> 00:32:39,900
We select the finest chocolate beans,

382
00:32:40,100 --> 00:32:41,880
predominantly the criollo bean,

383
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:43,400
which is the best-flavored bean,

384
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:46,400
and we grind them, roast them,

385
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:49,380
process them in a dedicated plant in Switzerland,

386
00:32:49,920 --> 00:32:53,060
and we ship out the chocolate mass

387
00:32:53,061 --> 00:32:54,560
in a one-metric-ton block,

388
00:32:55,280 --> 00:32:57,820
2,200 pounds of solid chocolate mass,

389
00:32:57,821 --> 00:32:59,540
to the manufacturing facilities.

390
00:33:02,560 --> 00:33:08,880
Lindstratham, New Hampshire plant makes the famous Lindor truffles, about 5.8 million

391
00:33:08,881 --> 00:33:15,780
of them per day.

392
00:33:15,781 --> 00:33:21,020
The mammoth block of Swiss-made chocolate liquor is hoisted into the liquor melter, where

393
00:33:21,021 --> 00:33:30,460
a series of 180-degree water-heated stainless steel rollers gently liquefy the solid mass.

394
00:33:30,461 --> 00:33:35,840
After nearly two hours, the product is ready to be combined with the dry ingredients, including

395
00:33:35,841 --> 00:33:38,840
sugar and milk powder, and then refined.

396
00:33:38,841 --> 00:33:43,140
We're putting together the ingredients here at the recipe tower.

397
00:33:43,141 --> 00:33:47,860
As we move down through this room, we're going to gradually reduce the particle size of the

398
00:33:47,861 --> 00:33:48,860
mix.

399
00:33:48,861 --> 00:33:51,780
At this point, the recipe is roughly 200 microns.

400
00:33:51,781 --> 00:33:54,700
It has roughly the consistency of a brownie mix.

401
00:33:54,701 --> 00:34:00,020
When we get done at the end of that process, we'll be in the 14 to 16 micron range.

402
00:34:00,021 --> 00:34:04,160
It's a range at which your mouth can no longer detect the particle size of the chocolate,

403
00:34:04,161 --> 00:34:08,580
which is really what differentiates premium chocolate from regular chocolate.

404
00:34:10,480 --> 00:34:17,000
Next, time for the conching, where the chocolate is gently rolled and blended for several hours to a smooth consistency.

405
00:34:18,100 --> 00:34:22,480
A process stumbled upon by this company's founder back in 1879.

406
00:34:22,481 --> 00:34:26,780
time.

407
00:34:26,781 --> 00:34:29,020
While experimenting with chocolate blending techniques

408
00:34:29,021 --> 00:34:33,120
